  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Palestinian Performing Arts Network (PPAN) 16-21 - Support to Performing Arts Nework 16-21</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Support to Performing Arts Network 16-21</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PPAN is the first Palestinian Performing Arts Network to be established in Palestine as an outcome of Sida&apos;s previous support to Abdel Mohsin Qattan Foundation during 2012-2015. The aim of this intervention is to strengthen performing arts capacities, further engage Young women, Children and youth in less privileged communities in performing arts and to bolster functionality, recognition and sustainability of an Active performing arts network.The results framework presented adequate indicators and targets and used the previous program baseline aiming to further develop it and improve it during the first year of the program while developing the monitoring system. The intervention total budget is 48 MSEK and Sida&apos;s share is 40 MSEK. The Network plans to diversity its fund base and decrease the support on Swedish through implementing the resource mobilisation strategy. The program budget designated 62% to the program activities, 22% for organisational development and 5.8% for admin cost. A resource mobilisation strategy is already in place and activated . Some donors are already approached during this year to support the Network .</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Palestinian Performing Arts Network, PPAN, har ans&#xf6;kt om ett st&#xf6;d uppg&#xe5;ende till 40,4 MSEK f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra ett program kallat &quot;Performing Art is a Right and an Entitlement&quot;, ungef&#xe4;r &quot;Scenkonst &#xe4;r en r&#xe4;ttighet&quot; under perioden 2016-2019.

Insatsen syftar till att bidra till utvecklingen av ett demokratiskt och pluralistiskt samh&#xe4;lle som respekterar m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rker den palestinska identiteten, s&#xe5;som den uppfattas av n&#xe4;tverkets medlemmar. Insatsen avser &#xf6;ka flickors och pojkars engagemang i scenkonstaktiviteter, s&#xe4;rskilt de som lever i marginaliserade och mindre priviligerade omr&#xe5;den som tex flyktingl&#xe4;gren i Gaza. PPANs medlemsorganisationer har en l&#xe5;ng erfarenhet av att arbeta f&#xf6;r  j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet mellan k&#xf6;nen och demokratiska v&#xe4;rden i utsatta omr&#xe5;den genom musik, dans, cirkus, teater mm. Insatsen genomf&#xf6;rs av n&#xe4;tverket PPAN och n&#xe4;tverkets medlemmar (11 st) i n&#xe4;ra samarbete. 

Medlemsorganisationerna planerar olika aktiviteter som finansieras via PPAN, som hanterar avtalsskrivande och utbetalning f&#xf6;r aktiviteter samt granskar redovisning och rapportering. 

Totalbudgeten uppg&#xe5;r till 48,4 MSEK, och PPAN avser s&#xf6;ka finaniering fr&#xe5;n andra givare uppg&#xe5;ende till 8 MSEK. Resterande 40,4 MSEK s&#xf6;ks fr&#xe5;n Sida.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall stated objective of PPAN programme is &quot;to contribute towards the development of a democratic and pluralistic society that respects human rights and enhances Palestinian national identity&quot;. PPAN&apos;s programme has defined three major outcomes that are well linked to a set of verifiable indicators, specific outputs and targets. The three outcomes are:

a) Functionality, recognition and sustainability of an active performing arts network are bolstered;
b) Young women, children and youth in less privileged communities are further engaged in performing arts and; 
c) Capacities of performing arts are strengthened, diversified and promoted at various levels.</narrative>
  </description>
